  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Alabama recorded $139M in federal contract obligations in FY2027 to date. The federal government made 316 awards in Alabama so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $441K. Obligations fell 99.2% year over year. The Department of Veterans Affairs accounted for the largest share of FY2027 to date obligations with $84.8M, followed by the National Aeronautics and Space Administration with $30.1M and the Department of Justice with $21.5M. AMERESCO INC led vendors with $52.3M in obligations, followed by PINTER MEMORIALS INC with $17.9M and NAPHCARE LLC with $17.8M. Engineering Services is the top industry in FY2027 to date with $54.2M in obligations, and General Medical and Surgical Hospitals and Cut Stone and Stone Product Manufacturing follow with $18M and $16.7M respectively. Earlier fiscal years show much larger totals, including $18.1B in FY25 and $17.6B in FY26, highlighting the current-year totals are partial and fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How do current obligations compare with recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "FY27 obligations stand at $139M compared with $17.6B in FY26 and $18.1B in FY25. FY24 obligations were $17.3B, FY23 obligations were $14.9B, and FY22 obligations were $14.1B. Obligations fell 99.2% year over year, and the note clarifies current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date)."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors dominate FY2027 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $84.8M, the National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $30.1M, and the Department of Justice obligated $21.5M in FY2027 to date. AMERESCO INC received $52.3M, PINTER MEMORIALS INC received $17.9M, and NAPHCARE LLC received $17.8M. Engineering Services is the largest industry with $54.2M, followed by General Medical and Surgical Hospitals with $18M and Cut Stone and Stone Product Manufacturing with $16.7M."
      }
    ]
